Description: Yu OS Framework platform services for Debian and Ubuntu
 Installs the Yu OS platform: `yu`, `yuosd`, `yuos-extension-host`, the
 system API and SDK/runtime libraries, capability and approval enforcement,
 audit/session persistence, the App host and its isolation, display, browser,
 nearby and semantic system services. Headless Apps and their common
 libraries are separately owned packages recommended through yuos-apps-agent.
 .
 The package also installs and enables the privileged `yuosd` system
 service. Ordinary Apps run in task-owned `yuos-extension-host` processes
 that `yuosd` supervises; none of them requires the Yu Agent. The official
 Yu Agent is the separate, optional `yuos-agent` package; without it, Agent
 features such as Agent tasks, triggers and Agent memory report that the Agent
 is not installed. Browser and user indexing services are installed but
 remain opt-in or condition-gated.
 OS desktop packages use its Root PAM display activation and supervised GUI
 transport helpers; their presence does not grant any App a GUI resource.
 It does not alter the host's home layout, boot identity, desktop
 environment, PAM policy, or firmware policy. Helium is optional on
 headless installs and required by the Browser App.
